## §9 — Condense
**Pattern (the wave's headline, §9 rule fired):** Amendment A13 — landed last cycle precisely to cure receipt incompleteness — met its first full wave, and **zero of five items cleared jev-prewave**. Every build passed its own mechanical checks (harness assertions all PASS on all five final builds; A6 legs at 0 HITs on four items, carried-with-disposition on the fifth) and every HOLD was ASSERTED-CHECKS on receipt grounds the judges verified as real: T199 (two index lines claiming evidence that did not exist — a probe never run, a color never printed) · T204 (endpoint receipts + swap moved-instant receipts for five checkpoints + a fit row filed as a product instead of a measured bbox) · T205 (a strict-bound receipt failing at exactly 0.30 with no receipt at that instant · a fixed "8000ms" label in place of an evaluated instant · census rows overstating two phases' runtime effect) · T208 (timing-swap movement evidence for seven checkpoints via the inputs each assertion actually reads · a guard-#2 geometry receipt under content swap) · T210 (a hold-dependent swap probe · one stale index line printing a superseded value against its own receipt · CP9 without a whole-state equality receipt · palette swap without observed output values). Own-checks dimension moved with cure rounds (0.25→0.40 · 0.35→0.40/0.45/0.48 · T199 0.40→0.70 across cycles) but never crossed. The defect is no longer enumeration (A13's index exists on every item and reconciliations were performed) — it is **receipt validity at the margin**: receipts that are present, plausible, and one predicate short of what their assertion prescribes, plus index lines whose claims outrun their receipts. The judges catch these reliably; the builders' self-reconciliation does not, because the same author writes the claim and checks it.

**Candidate amendment (filed, NOT landed — priced for HQ): RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE.** The A13 reconciliation gains a second pair of eyes: before the prewave payload is assembled, the receipt index is reconciled by a checker that did not author the build record — in this seat's form, a mechanical cross-check script where the assertion is mechanical (every CONFIG-expression receipt re-evaluated by script and diffed against the filed value; every claimed probe instant grepped in the filed raw output) plus the seat's spot re-probe of the index's highest-risk lines (swap receipts + endpoint receipts, the two classes named in three of this wave's five HOLDs). Evidence: 5 items, one wave, one defect class, against A13's own prediction (Cycle 036 §0b.1: the index "is priced to cut the re-fire count" — measured this wave: 9 prewave firings, 0 waves spent, 0 verdicts; the prediction failed on its first test and is recorded as failed). Landing form (instruction step · mechanical guard · Jev definition · Codex prompt) is HQ's pricing; this cycle files the candidate with its evidence and does not amend INSTRUCTION.md, because a second consecutive self-authored amendment to the same leg, landed the cycle after the first failed, is exactly the calibration-instead-of-pricing pattern the judgment-layer evaluation exists to catch. NOT-YET-AMENDED, consumer HQ.

**§0b dispositions:**
1. *T199 completion — DONE as charged, outcome NO VERDICT:* the authorized re-fire fired once, HOLDed on two overstated index lines (both judge-verified real; the builder recorded them as its own defects in scores.md). T199's further re-fire stands PENDING AUTHORIZATION (consumer HQ) under the Cycle-036 firing-3 reading — the NO-VERDICT pool awaiting authorization is now four items (T190 · T196 · T197 · T199), each with filed cures.
