**REVISE — Keep RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE at NOT-YET-AMENDED with HQ as consumer. Correct the evidence, layer dispositions, and cost accounting before closing §9.**

1. **The deferral is faithful. The causal claim exceeds the evidence.** A13 already requires every receipt to carry the evaluated CONFIG inputs and raw observed results its assertion demands. Wave 34 shows that the builder’s readiness check let deficient receipts reach jev-prewave on all five items. It does not establish that shared authorship caused the misses or that independence would have prevented them. Keep the candidate and name its owning surfaces, `INSTRUCTION.md` §5 leg 3b and the mechanical guard layer. Give HQ an explicit acceptance test against the filed failures. For example, T199’s A-8 requires checking the exact probe and window, B-17 requires checking the observed swapped color, and T205’s CP01 requires evaluating the binding predicate at its endpoint. Grepping for an instant and diffing CONFIG values alone would miss some of these. The HQ board still contains the Wave 34 Plan skeleton, so the handoff is named in §9 and remains unconfirmed on the board. [INSTRUCTION.md, A13.3](../../INSTRUCTION.md#amendment-a13) · [RUN.md, §9](RUN.md#9--condense) · [T199 completion return, findings 1–2](../../../../study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md) · [T205 re-fire, finding 1](../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md) · [HQ.json, Wave 34 entry](../../HQ.json)

2. **Mechanical guards need a complete disposition.** Command 4 was not demanded because there were no lens scores to consolidate. For commands 2, 6, and 7, distinguish sound requirements from deficient filed outputs. The T208 re-fire found no regenerated geometry result for command 2, T204’s swap-title fit row lacked a measured post-fit width for command 6, and T205’s census overstated runtime application for command 7. These support deferring a receipt-validation change with HQ. Merely producing an output does not prove the guard was satisfied. Correct the A6 summary as well. §5 records carried fit HITs for T199 and carried census HITs for T208, leaving **three** items with zero HITs on both legs. [guards.md, commands 2, 4, 6, 7](../../guards/guards.md#the-commands-mechanical-guards--callable-demonstrated) · [RUN.md, §§5 and 9](RUN.md) · [T208 re-fire, guard #2 finding](../../../../study/recreations/T208-paired-dot-counts-house-stage/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md) · [T204 re-fire, fit finding](../../../../study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md) · [T205 re-fire, finding 3](../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md)

3. **Jev and Codex coverage needs explicit treatment of the motion evidence.** The T204 Observe return requested continuous playback at Observe exit. The Execute receipt documents 32 frames inspected in sequence at 4 fps plus two source stills. T205’s Observe return independently requested continuous playback, and its amendment records decoded-frame probes. Neither record demonstrates the requested playback. Record T204’s advisory RETURN as set aside with the gap carried, unless a qualifying playback receipt can be cited. Price the Jev definition separately. Its §5 automatic floor is below 0.5, and the T204 return scored mechanics 0.5, so §9 needs to cite the applicable basis for RETURN or name the unresolved rule. Give the proposed FED-list change a reason for deferral. For `codex-observe`, explain whether motion verification was within scope and, if so, how its missed evidence is disposed. The four Plan REVISEs give affirmative evidence for the Plan reviews. The scoring prompt was unexercised, and the Condense prompt’s coverage rests on the filed review. [jev-observe-exit.md, §§1–5](../../guards/jev-observe-exit.md) · [T204 Observe return, Gate gap](jev-observe-exit-T204-return.md) · [T204 build record, Motion-viewing receipt](../../../../study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/build-record.md) · [T205 Observe return, Plan charges](jev-observe-exit-T205-return.md) · [T205 Plan amendment, Observe-exit charge 2](../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/plan-amendment-cycle037.md)

4. **Bind the lesson to the returns.** No five-lens score was produced, so the lens-score requirement does not fire. The lesson still uses Jev own-checks scores and findings. Put the exact `codex/` return paths beside each named progression and finding, including both T199 returns for its cross-cycle delta, instead of leaving §5’s aggregate summary as the citation. Qualify “judges verified as real” to reflect what each return checked. T204 and T210 describe paperwork reviews. T205 independently evaluated CP01 and found that the build failed the written strict bound, a stronger finding than a missing receipt. [RUN.md, §9 Pattern](RUN.md#9--condense) · [T199 prior re-fire](../../../../study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md) · [T199 completion re-fire](../../../../study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md) · [T205 re-fire, finding 1](../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md)

5. **Carry-forward is honest. The comparison needs correction.** Keep wave size and cadence **UNASSESSED** on measured per-item cost. Wave 34 records **25** Phase A, seat-gate, and prewave firings before Condense (`8 + 8 + 9`), or **26** including the first Condense call. The prewave HOLDs blocked all five scoring waves. Nine prewave firings establish where scoring stopped, while total cost remains unmeasured. Reconcile Cycle 036’s comparator before using it. Its listed components yield **19** under the same counting convention (`2 + 2 + 6 + 5 + 4`), while the HQ entry reports 18. The two cohorts also differ. Report that A13’s first full wave produced zero clearances and that its effect on re-fire frequency remains unestablished. [RUN.md, §9 disposition 6](RUN.md#9--condense) · [Cycle 036 RUN.md, §0b.1 disposition and Condense firing record](../2026-11-18-cycle-036-wave-33/RUN.md) · [HQ.json, Wave 33 entry](../../HQ.json)

